WEBVTT

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:05.190
<b>Episode 15: Amamiya Yuuhi and the Shinonome Brothers</b>

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.810
Is it good?

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:08.340
It's not very good.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:12.100
Hey! Yuu-kun!

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:12.900
Hmm?

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.930
You free the rest of today?

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.200
Want to work?

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.050
Work?

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.620
It pays 30,000 just to stand 
around wearing a suit.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.580
That's too shady.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:22.250
I'll do it.

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:24.250
At least be a little more suspicious!

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.910
Will Glasses here be all right?

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.900
He'll be fine.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.760
He's my brother's apprentice.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.310
He had an apprentice?

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.980
H-Hello.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:41.880
I'm Amamiya.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.360
I see.

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.900
That youngster took an apprentice, huh?

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:48.820
All right!

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.340
I'm counting on you today!

00:00:51.860 --> 00:00:53.860
Cut the damn crap!

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:55.650
Are you sure about that?

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:59.130
The Whirlwind's apprentice 
might not stay quiet.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.580
You got paid and yet your luxury 
is an 800-yen steak bento?

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.050
Leave me alone. Go home already.

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:12.740
Don't say that.

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:14.510
Demon's Lair

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:14.510
Let's drink together.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:18.030
I guess that's fine.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:20.120
Let's call the Princess, too! The Princess!

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:22.570
Sure, but she can't drink.

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:24.270
We have juice, too!

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:26.260
Cheers!

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:27.070
Mmn.

00:01:28.270 --> 00:01:29.760
Why's Anima here, too?

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:31.610
Couldn't stop her.

00:01:38.110 --> 00:01:40.120
Oh, you can drink, huh?

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.030
I heard you worked a job?

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:43.080
Yeah.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.790
They were calling Shinonome-san a youngster.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:50.250
Well, he was a young guy.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.960
I know,

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.650
but to me, he was the very model of an adult.

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.830
Well, even Aniki was considered 
a youngster in real society.

00:02:00.830 --> 00:02:02.880
I guess even we look like adults

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.050
from the perspective of Akane-kun, 
Subaru-chan, and Yuki-chan?

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.860
Maybe so.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.810
When I was about Subaru's age, 
Aniki was a college student.

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:18.690
Shinonome-san when he was our age, huh?

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:20.730
I can't even imagine it.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.990
I can't imagine Mi-kun 
as a middle schooler, either.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:27.300
Shall I tell you, then?

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:28.310
I want to hear!

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:31.370
Back when I had just 
started middle school...

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:49.530
<i>When I looked up, 
that sky was full of wonders.</i>

00:02:49.530 --> 00:02:54.830
<i>The despair I bottled up tormented me,</i>

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:58.800
<i>and I wanted the courage 
to break my chains of isolation.</i>

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.070
<i>(You are my light)</i>

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:05.660
<i>I was searching for your 
brilliant light in my hazy dreams</i>

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.960
<i>to kick away the limits placed on myself.</i>

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.920
<i>Now with your courage, 
let’s soar into the sky.</i>

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.630
<i>Let's CRUSH the fear!</i>

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:22.770
<i>I swear to you, at the ends 
of this chaotic world,</i>

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.310
<i>that even if you fall, I'll</i>

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:27.860
<i>Be the HERO!</i>

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:33.040
<i>I'll be waiting at the future 
we're moving toward,</i>

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.930
<i>with a “YES, MY LORD!” 
for your constant radiance,</i>

00:03:36.930 --> 00:03:41.000
<i>clutching the stars raining down upon us.</i>

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:48.620
<i>I'll love you until we reach 
that future you want to destroy.</i>

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:07.080
Aniki, Aniki!

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:10.310
Today I beat six third-years!

00:04:10.310 --> 00:04:13.330
What was the most you beat 
at one time, Aniki?

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:14.960
Twenty billion.

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:16.400
Y-You liar!

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:18.330
Mikazuki,

00:04:18.330 --> 00:04:20.830
being strong in a fight won't land you a job.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:23.330
Though I guess that doesn't matter.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.990
You are dumb!

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:28.580
Grr! Come to the dojo! It's a duel!

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:36.000
What kind of sound was that?

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.700
Damn it!

00:04:37.700 --> 00:04:41.200
If I was the same age and build 
as you, I would definitely win!

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.670
In that case,

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:47.180
once you reach my current age, 
I'll fight you seriously.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.060
<i>You mean you weren't serious just now?</i>

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:02.900
<i>There's no way a guy who just 
lazes around could be that strong.</i>

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:06.980
<i>There definitely has to be 
some secret to it!</i>

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:09.810
He's gone?!

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.130
That's strange.

00:05:13.130 --> 00:05:14.380
Hey, you.

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:17.000
Why were you stalking that guy?

00:05:17.530 --> 00:05:19.430
Someone asked you to tail him, right?

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:21.230
Not telling.

00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:23.530
How much did they pay you?

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:27.030
I'll double it if you tell us.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:32.300
Wha?!

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:36.040
Try forcing it out of me!

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:37.920
This damn brat!

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:40.780
Here I go!

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:53.420
Crazy brat.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:54.970
He's still got that damn smile.

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.830
Hey, this the one?

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:59.510
It seemed like he had some 
connection to that man,

00:05:59.510 --> 00:06:00.650
so we captured him.

00:06:01.070 --> 00:06:03.420
A connection to the Whirlwind, huh?

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.510
Whirlwind?

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:05.800
His nickname.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:07.900
If you try to surround him,

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:10.850
then people start flying like they 
were sucked into a whirlwind.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:13.510
Why the hell are you laughing?!

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.730
Hurry up and spill what you know!

00:06:16.730 --> 00:06:19.380
<i>Aniki really is incredible!</i>

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:22.640
<i>He's got these damn adults frightened 
of him and using a nickname for him!</i>

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.090
What a creepy brat.

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:29.430
Um, excuse me.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:35.320
Kidnapping a kid makes you 
bad people, you know?

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:37.480
Who the hell are you?!

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:42.140
I'm the super hero, Masked Hangetsu!

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:45.120
It's the Whirlwind! Don't fight fair!

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:46.950
Bust his legs! His legs!

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:49.350
Don't kill him!

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:53.060
We need him to sing 
about whoever's backing him!

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:55.490
I'll bring you to your knees!

00:06:58.580 --> 00:06:59.660
Why, you!

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.020
S-Stop!

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:09.190
You bastard!

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.400
Why were you tailing me?

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:22.750
Because you went after my men!

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:27.100
That was because you all went 
and bothered normal civilians.

00:07:27.100 --> 00:07:29.300
I was just giving you a warning.

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.970
Hey!

00:07:30.970 --> 00:07:34.180
Masked Hanketsu, the fuzz 
is on the way, so let's scram.

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:37.890
It's Hangetsu, not Hanketsu.

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:40.100
Hanketsu!

00:07:40.100 --> 00:07:42.180
You're getting a spanking later.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:43.820
Huh?! In this day and age?!

00:07:48.940 --> 00:07:51.900
Jeez, what were you doing?

00:07:53.290 --> 00:07:57.410
I was searching for the secret 
behind your strength so I can surpass you!

00:07:57.410 --> 00:07:58.530
You idiot!

00:07:58.530 --> 00:08:00.950
This wasn't some fight between children.

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:04.080
I didn't do anything. 
I was strong from the start.

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:05.710
L-Liar!

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.840
And who's the old dude?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.300
I do trouble-shooting, security,

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:14.550
and well, I'm basically a handyman.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.940
So you're the one backing Aniki!

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:18.510
Let me work for you, too!

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.770
Listen, you.

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:23.180
If anything, this job is 
about stopping fights.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:26.100
Why do you want to surpass 
your brother so badly?

00:08:29.740 --> 00:08:31.990
Because the mountain is there!

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:34.490
The mountain, huh?

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:36.450
No logic behind it?

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.330
I'm sure he has his own logic.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:43.160
He probably wants your approval, you know?

00:08:43.470 --> 00:08:46.650
He really, really respects you.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:49.880
Mikazuki.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.220
What?

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:54.240
Take the proper steps before you right now.

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:57.390
You don't race up mountains, 
you take the time to climb them.

00:08:57.390 --> 00:08:59.730
How can I take it that slowly?!

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.970
I want to get stronger than you!

00:09:02.440 --> 00:09:03.730
Then do it.

00:09:04.970 --> 00:09:06.570
I know you can.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.090
I'll be looking forward to it.

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:13.360
Yeah! Just you wait!

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.410
I will surpass you!

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:23.120
<b>6 Years Later</b>

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:28.290
So strong...

00:09:28.750 --> 00:09:31.500
I feel like you're getting 
even farther away.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:32.900
Mikazuki,

00:09:32.900 --> 00:09:35.220
you want to try working now?

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:35.940
Huh?!

00:09:35.940 --> 00:09:37.810
I do! Leave it to me!

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:39.600
Aniki...

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:42.110
Were you holding back this time, too?

00:09:42.680 --> 00:09:46.470
I went all out, to celebrate 
you getting into college.

00:09:46.940 --> 00:09:49.560
So? That mountain still high?

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:52.650
Yeah, looks like I'll be able 
to enjoy it for a while.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:53.530
Hmm?

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:56.730
Congratulations on passing.

00:09:57.490 --> 00:09:59.980
You've grown strong, Mikazuki.

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:06.170
So yeah, he was like that.

00:10:09.150 --> 00:10:10.690
Huh?! She's asleep?!

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:13.140
The Princess tried her best to listen,

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:17.030
but she got dizzier with 
every drink Anima downed.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:19.840
Well, whatever.

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:21.620
That was a great story.

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.180
Thanks!

00:10:23.550 --> 00:10:25.150
You okay, Neu?

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:27.780
Are you not feeling the effects 
of Yuu-kun's liquor?

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:29.890
I'm feeling a little unsteady.

00:10:31.410 --> 00:10:32.410
Mikazuki.

00:10:33.670 --> 00:10:35.220
Want to do it this weekend?

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:36.230
Do what?

00:10:36.640 --> 00:10:39.320
The rematch of our duel.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:44.600
Now that's rare!

00:10:44.600 --> 00:10:47.370
Never expected you to bring it up, Yuu-kun.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.290
Did hearing about my brother 
get you fired up?

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:51.560
What are you talking about?

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.340
Yuuhi's always been hot-blooded.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:57.200
Well, I am the Whirlwind's apprentice.

00:10:57.200 --> 00:10:58.620
So, how about it?

00:10:59.460 --> 00:11:01.330
Yeah. You're on.

00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:02.400
All right.

00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:06.140
Then whoever wins gets a date with Samidare.

00:11:06.140 --> 00:11:07.140
Huh?!

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:10.690
I can't afford to lose.

00:11:11.060 --> 00:11:14.030
You brought it up because 
you think you can win, right?

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:15.260
Not sure.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:17.030
That's worrying.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:22.950
I figured, either way, I'll have to fight 
Mikazuki a few times moving forward.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.550
Why's that?

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:30.920
Because it's necessary.

00:11:36.670 --> 00:11:39.650
Um, you look like you're in a good mood.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:40.970
Hm?

00:11:42.440 --> 00:11:44.430
I've got a date this weekend.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:45.090
Huh?!

00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:46.270
W-With who?!

00:11:46.270 --> 00:11:47.350
With Yuu-kun.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:51.450
Y-You mean for like a martial arts match?

00:11:51.450 --> 00:11:53.400
Yeah, that.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:55.050
You berserker!

00:11:55.050 --> 00:11:57.210
If you pick a fight 
with Subaru, I'll kill you!

00:11:57.210 --> 00:11:58.770
Ly, stop it!

00:11:58.770 --> 00:12:02.380
I-If you pick a fight with Yukimachi,

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:05.480
I-I won't stand for it.

00:12:05.790 --> 00:12:07.690
Long, it's fine.

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:12.030
You say something to him, too, Mu!

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:18.970
I see Mu's as silent as ever.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:21.380
He does talk on occasion, though.

00:12:22.270 --> 00:12:24.920
The last time we spoke was...

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:28.210
Oh, yeah, when I made my wish.

00:12:28.890 --> 00:12:31.480
What kind of nonsense did you wish for?

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.360
Ly!

00:12:34.640 --> 00:12:37.450
That was back when 
I was wandering around India.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:39.860
There was this kid dancing.

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:04.650
I didn't have anything on me to give her, so...

00:13:13.110 --> 00:13:14.770
B-Bread?!

00:13:14.770 --> 00:13:16.940
That's all you used it on?!

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.000
Yeah.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.420
I-I can't believe it.

00:13:20.420 --> 00:13:21.900
You're crazy.

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:24.150
What did you two wish for?

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:26.110
Well, um...

00:13:26.760 --> 00:13:29.110
Sorry, that's a secret.

00:13:29.410 --> 00:13:31.220
Hm?

00:13:31.220 --> 00:13:32.500
Well, whatever.

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:39.380
Setting that aside, we're really 
struggling to find Animus, huh?

00:13:40.970 --> 00:13:42.880
Hey, Maimakterion.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.590
I'm leaving the books here.

00:13:50.360 --> 00:13:52.140
What a strange one.

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:54.270
Do golems even read books?

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:58.850
Everything from textbooks to manga, 
with no preference, either?

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.200
These are strange, too.

00:14:02.200 --> 00:14:05.020
They're not very strong, 
so they're not that scary.

00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:08.910
Really? I think they're scary enough.

00:14:13.070 --> 00:14:15.600
It was born out of nothing?!

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:20.500
Hoo... So that's the trick 
behind it popping up over and over.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:27.890
Wha?!

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:30.550
Oh, leaving already?

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:31.430
Animus?!

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:35.060
Then go have fun, Pyanepsion.

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:44.100
This presence...

00:14:44.100 --> 00:14:46.210
So those really were the tenth one.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:07.050
Princess!

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:14.390
Asahina, can you fight?

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:15.970
I'm in perfect form!

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:22.120
There're always so many of them.

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:25.390
Hakudou-san and Shinonome-kun's 
wide-area attacks

00:15:25.390 --> 00:15:27.280
weren't able to deal a decisive blow.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:31.300
In cases such as these, isn't there usually 
a main body or a core somewhere?

00:15:31.300 --> 00:15:34.990
There's no precedent 
of a golem having a weak point,

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:38.590
but it looks like our usual 
brute force won't work here.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.880
Now, how will you fight them?

00:15:45.880 --> 00:15:50.550
If you space out, you'll get overwhelmed 
by their numbers and slowly killed off.

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.880
It's simple!

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:56.190
We smash them all!

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:57.140
Huh?!

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:14.820
<i>Ahh, how beautiful.</i>

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:18.080
I could die here.

00:16:19.320 --> 00:16:22.130
<i>We think alike, Mikazuki.</i>

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:33.700
Impossible!

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.500
It's over already?

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:37.400
No way.

00:16:37.400 --> 00:16:39.090
I couldn't see it at all.

00:16:52.930 --> 00:16:57.200
The park you'll be 
dueling in is all mud now.

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:00.890
That kills the excitement.

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.680
Maybe I can change it to next—

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:08.060
No rain checks.

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:08.060
<i>No rain checks.</i>

00:17:08.840 --> 00:17:14.550
Yuuhi, you know dueling in the rain 
sets a pretty nice scene.

00:17:14.550 --> 00:17:16.280
Well, I guess so.

00:17:16.910 --> 00:17:18.100
What, what?!

00:17:18.100 --> 00:17:19.530
Where am I?!

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:24.850
That's our Anima-sama!

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.180
What a thoughtful arrangement!

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:30.990
It is nice, but still irritating.

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:35.260
Since the Princess forbade personal fights, 
I'm glad she put her to sleep,

00:17:35.780 --> 00:17:37.760
but why bring her at all, then?

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:42.280
This is a pretty great spot!

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:44.700
Yuu-kun, let's get started already!

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:45.870
Yeah.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:58.130
Aerial Domain!

00:18:18.540 --> 00:18:19.680
I can see them!

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:21.370
I can see them better than before!

00:18:22.380 --> 00:18:23.550
This is great!

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:26.580
You're putting your soul into your 
movements, unlike last time!

00:18:33.320 --> 00:18:34.170
<i>What...</i>

00:18:35.470 --> 00:18:36.860
<i>is this feeling?</i>

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.670
Well?! How are you feeling?!

00:18:40.550 --> 00:18:42.020
Awesome!

00:18:42.020 --> 00:18:43.570
Me, too!

00:18:44.780 --> 00:18:47.170
Oh, boy. So weak.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:52.100
I mean, do you even know what you 
want to do in the first place, Yuu-kun?

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:55.650
<i>That's right.</i>

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:57.780
<i>What I want to do is important.</i>

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:59.420
<i>Step forward and believe in the results!</i>

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:03.830
<i>I'm sure Shinonome-san always fought 
like he was challenging someone.</i>

00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:05.620
<i>Forward! Forward!</i>

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.540
<i>Mikazuki, you're strong.</i>

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:16.090
<i>I respect you.</i>

00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:38.100
That's enough, match is over.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:44.440
Those two are great.

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:45.610
I could fall for them.

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:00.220
My dojo, huh?

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:04.810
I was always left sprawled out like this.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:12.310
So? That mountain still high?

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:17.070
Yeah, looks like I'll be able 
to enjoy it for a while.

00:20:35.080 --> 00:20:36.340
Mikazuki-san.

00:20:36.340 --> 00:20:36.830
Hm?

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:37.940
Hey!

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:40.450
How did your match go yesterday?

00:20:41.300 --> 00:20:43.010
I completely lost!

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:46.220
You seem awfully happy for someone who lost.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:49.750
Festivals are more fun 
when they're longer, right?

00:20:49.750 --> 00:20:52.050
S-Sure?

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:53.940
That's basically it!

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:59.610
I guess Yuu-kun's on a date 
with the Princess right now.

00:20:59.610 --> 00:21:04.320
You were betting a d-date on the match?

00:21:04.320 --> 00:21:08.660
Well, yeah. Tch. Lucky Yuu-kun.

00:21:08.660 --> 00:21:10.130
What are you talking about?

00:21:10.130 --> 00:21:10.970
Huh?

00:21:10.970 --> 00:21:14.160
You've got a pretty girl 
for each arm, don't you?

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:20.610
That's true!

00:21:20.610 --> 00:21:22.510
You two want to go have fun somewhere?

00:21:22.770 --> 00:21:24.400
I-I don't have any money.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:26.980
Dummy, it's my treat.

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:34.630
Excuse me! I'd like to order more!

00:21:35.130 --> 00:21:37.370
Why is Anima here, too?!

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:43.580
Everyone, listen up as Shimaki talks 
about Animus's golems.

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:46.870
When the seven-eyed golem appeared,

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:49.070
Animus apparently called it Hekatombaion.

00:21:49.470 --> 00:21:54.800
Hekatombaion means the month roughly 
stretching from late July to early August.

00:21:54.800 --> 00:21:57.860
He probably meant for that name 
to mean it was his seventh one.

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:01.070
He also told us at the time 
we were in the middle stretch.

00:22:01.540 --> 00:22:05.450
If number seven puts us in the middle, 
and they're named after months,

00:22:05.450 --> 00:22:08.510
then we can presume that 
the total number of golems

00:22:08.510 --> 00:22:10.400
is equal to the number of months.

00:22:11.630 --> 00:22:13.010
Twelve.

00:22:13.670 --> 00:22:17.150
It's the same number of Knights, 
so I'm fairly certain.

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:21.290
With the ninth defeated, only three remain.

00:22:21.890 --> 00:22:23.870
We're entering the final stretch!

00:22:23.870 --> 00:22:27.280
Everyone, be sure to hone 
your techniques even more!

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:28.290
That's all!

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:33.680
<i>Once we stop the Biscuit Hammer, 
will Amamiya-kun...</i>

00:22:35.030 --> 00:22:36.470
<i>really...</i>

00:22:39.640 --> 00:22:40.770
Princess.

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:49.720
<i>Only three left.</i>

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:27.480
<b>Next Episode:
Yukimachi and Subaru</b>
